  "id": "Compound::DB00477 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Chlorpromazine, a phenothiazine antipsychotic, is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Chlorpromazine, as part of the phenothiazine class, binds to Cyp3a4, with Prochlorperazine, a member of this class, also exhibiting a binding interaction with Cyp3a4. This binding is supported by multiple paths, which highlight a consistent mechanism of action involving the enzyme Cyp3a4. The presence of a lowest common ancestor at the phenothiazine class indicates a shared biological pathway, suggesting that the interaction between Chlorpromazine and Cyp3a4 may be mediated through a common functional component. The evidence also indicates that Chlorpromazine may contribute to the pathophysiology of conditions like Colon Atonic and Pill Rolling, which are associated with Cyp3a4. These findings support a mechanistic link between Chlorpromazine and Cyp3a4, particularly through the enzyme's role in drug metabolism. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Cyp3a4 in the pharmacological effects of Chlorpromazine, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
